$attach_audio — mux audio onto video

SUMMARY
  Combines each videos[] clip with a sounds[] track (video stream copied, new audio).

SYNTAX
  $attach_audio
  @out: (@clip, @music) -> $attach_audio -> $save('final.mp4')
  $attach_audio(shortest=0)

INPUT
  videos[] — required
  sounds[] — required

OUTPUT
  videos[] — one MP4 per pair (only videos[] in the output bundle)

PAIRING
  Equal counts — zip video[i] with sound[i]
  One video, N sounds — same video with each sound
  N videos, one sound — each video with the same sound

ARGUMENTS
  shortest=    — 1/true (default): trim to shorter stream
  audio_codec= — ffmpeg audio encoder (default aac)

DEPENDENCIES
  ffmpeg + ffprobe: uv run python tools/download_ffmpeg.py  (→ tools/ffmpeg/)
  or system install on PATH

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_ATTACH_AUDIO=1 — stub .mp4 links without ffmpeg

EXAMPLE
  @clip: $file('silent.mp4')
  @music: $file('track.wav')
  @final: (@clip, @music) -> $attach_audio -> $save('out.mp4')

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No — output is videos[] only (sounds[] and other arrays cleared).
